STUDIO SCRIPT V1 validate + review (Next.js) — patch 04
=========================================================

ORDERING: apply ON TOP OF patch 01
(01-universal-preflight-and-production-api.patch) — this patch wires
into the Unified Pipeline section and preflight state that 01 adds to
app/page.tsx, so apply 01 first. Independent of patches 02/03
(affiliate workspace / link-paste input): no shared files.

  git apply ai_clip_studio/frontend_patches/01-universal-preflight-and-production-api.patch
  git apply ai_clip_studio/frontend_patches/04-studio-script-v1-validate-review.patch

WHAT IT ADDS (same surface as the :8788 server UI, Vietnamese labels):
- app/api/production/validate/route.ts (new): proxies POST {script} to
  the :8788 backend /api/production/validate, passing status/body
  through unchanged (including 422 with the line-numbered error list).
- components/ScriptReviewPanel.tsx (new): "Kiểm tra kịch bản V1"
  button + review panel rendering the validate response generically
  (characters/locations/props/scenes/shots/narration/dialogue/cues,
  storytelling mode + primary character + EXTERNAL_NARRATOR status and
  the 0-external-narrator-lines count, meta, end card, QA expected
  counts, OUTPUT/Drive, unsupported fields, line-numbered errors).
- app/page.tsx: renders the panel after PreflightPanel; the Unified
  Pipeline "Tạo Draft" button stays disabled while the current script
  text is a V1 script that failed validation. Free-form scripts are
  never blocked; the backend still refuses invalid V1 server-side.

No backend endpoint is invented: the validate endpoint is the one the
:8788 ai_clip_studio server already serves, plus the existing
analyze/preflight/draft endpoints. Full `npm run build` / `npm run
lint` still needs to run on Windows (node_modules are not in the repo).

